## 1. Why this error happens

### Error:

```text
Function float clsInputValidate::ReadFloatNumber(string ErrorMessage) has already been declared with return type double
```

C++ **does not allow overloading by return type only**.

So these two are considered the **same function**, not two overloads:

```cpp
static double ReadFloatNumber(string ErrorMessage = "Invalid Number, Enter again\n");
static float ReadFloatNumber(string ErrorMessage = "Invalid Number, Enter again\n");
```

The parameter list is the same:

```cpp
string ErrorMessage
```

Only the return type changed, and that is not enough for overloading.

---

## 2. Why the default argument error happens

### Error:

```text
Redefinition of default argument for parameter 'ErrorMessage'
```

This happens if you write the default value more than once, for example:

```cpp
static float ReadFloatNumber(string ErrorMessage = "Invalid Number, Enter again\n");

float clsInputValidate::ReadFloatNumber(string ErrorMessage = "Invalid Number, Enter again\n")
{
    // ...
}
```

Default arguments should be written **only once**, usually in the declaration.

