The **“Unexpected identifier”** errors around lines **166–177** are most likely caused by this syntax:

```cpp
__declspec(property(get = GetUserName, put = SetUserName)) string UserName;
```

That is a **Microsoft Visual C++ extension**. You’re using **CLion on Linux**, which usually compiles with **GCC/Clang**, and they do **not support `__declspec(property)`**.

So the compiler sees `__declspec(property(...))` and gets confused, producing **Unexpected identifier** errors.

## Fix

Remove the `__declspec(property...)` lines and use normal getter/setter functions instead.

