The main issue in the shown `clsUser.h` is that the code uses **`UserName`** and **`Password`** as if they are public properties, but your class only has private members:

```cpp
string _UserName;
string _Password;
```

and public getter functions:

```cpp
string GetUserName()
string GetPassword()
```

So these lines are wrong:

```cpp
if (U.GetUserName() == UserName)
```

`UserName` here is not declared in that scope.

And these are also wrong:

```cpp
if (User.UserName == UserName)
```

```cpp
if (User.UserName == UserName && User.Password == Password)
```

```cpp
if (U.UserName == _UserName)
```

There is no public member named `UserName` or `Password`.

Use the private fields inside the class, or use the getters.

For example:

<llm-snippet-file>include/Screens/ManageUsers/clsUser.h</llm-snippet-file>
