```

## Important note

If you change `Withdraw` from:

```c++
void Withdraw(double Amount)
```

to:

```c++
bool Withdraw(double Amount)
```

then every place that calls `Withdraw()` will still work, even if it ignores the returned value:

```c++
Client1.Withdraw(Amount);
```

That is allowed in C++.

So yes, changing `void` to `bool` is a clean solution.

