Great 

The error happens because:

```text
cls
```

is a **Windows command**.

On Linux, the command is:

```text
clear
```

So instead of using:

```cpp
system("cls");
```

you should use a small cross-platform function.

## 1. Add a clear-screen function in `clsScreen.h`

Since all your screens inherit from `clsScreen`, this is the best place.

<llm-snippet-file>include/clsScreen.h</llm-snippet-file>
```cpp
#pragma once
#include <iostream>
#include <cstdlib>
#include "Manage_Users_Screen/clsUser.h"
#include "Global.h"

using namespace std;

class clsScreen
{
protected :
    static void _ClearScreen()
    {
#ifdef _WIN32
        system("cls");
#else
        system("clear");
#endif
    }

    static void _DrawScreenHeader(string Title,string SubTitle ="")
    {
        cout << "\t\t\t\t\t______________________________________";
        cout << "\n\n\t\t\t\t\t  " << Title;
// ... existing code ...
```

## 2. Replace `system("cls")` with `_ClearScreen()`

For example, in `clsLoginScreen.h`:

<llm-snippet-file>include/clsLoginScreen.h</llm-snippet-file>
```cpp
// ... existing code ...
public:
    static void ShowLoginScreen()
    {
        _ClearScreen();
        _DrawScreenHeader("\t  Login Screen");
        _Login();
    }
};
#endif //PROJECT1L4BANKEXTENSION2_CLSLOGINSCREEN_H
```

