```

The program **is entering**, but because you logged in with:

```text
User1
1234
```

this user has permissions:

```text
0
```

So when you choose menu options like `1`, `2`, `3`, etc., your program calls `CheckAccessRights(...)`, finds that `User1` has **no access**, then returns back to the main menu.

That is why it looks like “nothing happened”.

## Test with full access user

Login with:

```text
User2
1234
```

`User2` has permission:

```text
-1
```

which means full access.

Then choosing `1`, `2`, `6`, `7`, etc. should work better.

---

